# shellcheck shell=bash
# direnv: enter the pinned dev shell automatically, so the tools you get are
# the tools CI gets. Entering also installs the git hooks (SPEC V17).
#
# nix-direnv rebuilds the cached shell only when `flake.nix`, `flake.lock`
# or this file changes, but the shell itself is defined under `nix/`, so
# watch those too or edits to them are silently ignored. The shell hook is
# read into the shell by `builtins.readFile`, so it counts as shell source.
watch_file nix/*.nix
watch_file scripts/dev/shell-hook.sh
use flake
